Mainline mici firmware provenance
================================

SOURCES.json identifies the additional firmware used by this port. Every
listed file was compared byte-for-byte with the specified source revision.
SHA256SUMS paths are relative to /usr/lib/firmware. To verify an installed
image:

  cd /usr/lib/firmware
  sha256sum -c /usr/share/doc/mainline-firmware/SHA256SUMS

These are provenance records, not a replacement license for the firmware.
The original notices in licenses/ apply only to the files assigned to them
in SOURCES.json. They do not establish coverage for other similarly named
blobs, device extracts, or board-data modifications.

Verified upstream distributions
-------------------------------

Linux-firmware revision 59f9fc2ef8d1e312d2a613d4e1ffad2ff31a0a01:
https://gitlab.com/kernel-firmware/linux-firmware/-/tree/59f9fc2ef8d1e312d2a613d4e1ffad2ff31a0a01

The revision's WHENCE assigns firmware-5.bin to
LICENSE.QualcommAtheros_ath10k. It assigns the matching A630 SQE/GMU,
SDM845 MBA/modem images and ADSP/CDSP/modemuw JSON maps to LICENSE.qcom
and NOTICE.qcom. The original files are copied unchanged into licenses/.
The GMU alias resolves to an unchanged file already shipped by AGNOS.

Wireless-regdb revision e05260afb7203dd0a7ba6faf9a30c86faf19a24e:
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/wens/wireless-regdb.git/commit/?id=e05260afb7203dd0a7ba6faf9a30c86faf19a24e

Both regulatory.db and its signature match this revision, tagged
master-2025-07-10. Its original LICENSE is licenses/wireless-regdb-LICENSE.

Device-specific files whose notice coverage remains unverified
-------------------------------------------------------------

The following files exactly match commaai/vamos revision
7626c378c3d5762df673dd14d457631057779d27 under kernel/firmware/:
https://github.com/commaai/vamos/tree/7626c378c3d5762df673dd14d457631057779d27/kernel/firmware

* ath10k/WCN3990/hw1.0/wlanmdsp.mbn:
  vamos commit 9869d6e05200cb24ad403da110fc9ec620fe972e identifies it as
  the device's /firmware/image/wlanmdsp.mbn, version
  WLAN.HL.2.0.c10-00459-QCAHLSWMTPLZ-1. It differs from the upstream
  linux-firmware image checked above. No license notice accompanying this
  device-extracted version was found in the import.

* ath10k/WCN3990/hw1.0/board-2.bin:
  The same commit appends variant=comma-mici and variant=comma-tizi entries
  to the generic board container. Their payloads exactly match the
  pre-existing AGNOS /usr/comma/wlan/bdwlan.b01 and bdwlan.b00, respectively:
    b01 SHA256 34757421765ee3bf9e57eafe59ea47b7c645918b7699753bcfebe31144ba76e7
    b00 SHA256 52812b95b0ff0aedd0f9f55e21e80fb39057158d91c0b94845c52a3bbbc48e50
  The source history identifies the custom board data but does not supply
  its original redistribution notice. The generic upstream ath10k notice
  is not asserted to license these modifications.

* qca/crbtfw11.tlv, crbtfw20.tlv, crbtfw21.tlv,
  crnv11.bin, crnv20.bin and crnv21.bin:
  vamos commit d38d75f7209c49777cd9b9a47db3b90dc7d2268a imports these six
  files without an upstream revision or redistribution notice. They were
  not found as identical files in the linux-firmware revision above.

* qcom/sdm845/modemr.jsn:
  Imported by vamos commit f6f7978442a1381f6e9458b238061a9a868b366c.
  This exact path is absent in the checked upstream linux-firmware tree,
  and the import does not identify a separate notice for it.

Original redistribution notices for these files still need to be located;
no license coverage is inferred from their names or from other firmware.
This directory records the unresolved status explicitly.

Existing vendor firmware and runtime calibration
------------------------------------------------

The existing AGNOS a630_zap.elf is exposed through a mainline-compatible
symlink. The remaining vendor audio/video firmware is loaded from the
existing /firmware/image partition. Their redistribution notices have not
been re-audited by this provenance update; no replacement images are added.
Panel gamma bytes are generated at boot from each device's persist data.
